# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. Nothing here ever enters history.
#
# `Keys/` holds a SCREENSHOT of a HyperLiquid API key. A committed secret is not
# removed by deleting it later - it stays in every clone of the history - so it
# is excluded before the first commit rather than cleaned up after one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Keys/
.env
*.env
!*.env.example
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*credential*
*secret*
!.conda/Lib/secrets.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE LEDGERS. Derived, private, and rebuildable.
#
# `transactions` is the immutable source of truth, but these files also carry a
# real financial position. Version-controlling them would put balances into a
# history that may one day be pushed somewhere, and would conflict on every run.
# Back them up; do not commit them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Broker and exchange exports - trade history, account identifiers.
#
# `**/` PREFIXES, BECAUSE A PATTERN WITH A SLASH IS ANCHORED TO THIS FILE'S
# DIRECTORY. `data/odds_drops/` matched only <root>/data/odds_drops/ and never
# Sports_Desk/data/odds_drops/ - the first real odds drop showed up as untracked
# and would have been committed by `git add -A`. Every desk keeps its data under
# its own `data/`, so every rule here must match at any depth.
#
# `data/imports/*` rather than `data/imports/` so the samples folder and the
# README can be re-included - git cannot re-include inside an excluded
# directory, only inside an excluded glob.
**/data/imports/*
!**/data/imports/README.txt
!**/data/imports/samples/
**/data/processed/
**/data/failed/
**/data/odds_drops/
**/data/results_drops/
**/data/polymarket_drops/
*_trades.csv
*_liquidations.csv
binance*.csv
binanceus*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environments and caches. `.conda` alone is large enough to hang `du`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.conda/
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS and agent scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
*.tmp
scratch/
.agents/
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `quant_trading_lab` HAS ITS OWN GIT REPOSITORY.
#
# Staged from here it becomes a gitlink - a bare pointer - and its 171-test
# codebase is NOT tracked by this repo at all. That is the worst outcome: it
# looks version-controlled and is not. It already versions itself, so this repo
# stays out of its way rather than shadowing it with an empty reference.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
quant_trading_lab/

# Obsidian vault - notes, synced separately, and noisy in a diff.
obsidian_vault/.obsidian/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state (Round 36). PID lock files and the supervisor's JSONL log are
# rewritten on every start; they were tracked by the Round 26 baseline and
# churned in every diff. Untracked with `git rm --cached` and ignored here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pid
*.jsonl

# Runtime paper state, discovered-user lists, caches and backups (Round 37).
# All of these are rewritten by running processes and were tracked only because
# the Round 26 baseline was a snapshot of a live working tree.
basis_paper_state.json
collector_status.json
collector.log
collector.log.1
cross_market/titan_identities_cache.json
paper_trading_state.json
hyperliquidusers.txt
**/data/cache/*
*.bak
# Round 63: paper dutch receipts (cross_market.execution_log --paper) are runtime data
**/data/paper_receipts/
# Round 73 review: detached loop logs (watcher, cross-market exporter)
**/data/*.log
# Round 85: C2 bot runtime state and the emergency sentinel (operator state, never committed)
cross_market/data/c2_bot_offset.json
HALT.flag
# Round 87: recorded CLOB book stamps (research data, never committed)
cross_market/data/clob_books/
# Round 116: live dress-rehearsal scratch (books, a vault copy, synthetic event, curve) - never committed
cross_market/data/rehearsals/

# Round 103b: cross_market/data holds RUNTIME artifacts and operator batch files. A broad
# `git add cross_market/` swept five of them into a commit, including fomc_drill_2026-09-16.bat
# which AGENTS.md documents as "operator file, untracked, CRLF". Registrations live in
# cross_market/experiments/ and stay tracked; nothing under data/ does.
cross_market/data/*.json
cross_market/data/*.bat
cross_market/data/*.log
cross_market/data/*.pid

# Round 107 (Ruling R95-E): three EXPORTER-WRITTEN dashboards that a live daemon rewrites on a
# 15-second cycle. They dirtied `git status` on every round and were never anyone's edit, so the
# diffs carried no information - the durable record lives in wiki/regimes/, wiki/experiments/ and
# wiki/desks/, which the knowledge layer owns and lints.
#
# ONLY THESE THREE. Monarch_Hub.md is also exporter-written but stays TRACKED: five wiki pages link
# it, and lint L8 resolves wikilinks against files on disk, so untracking it would make a fresh
# clone fail L8 with five dangling links. Verified before untracking: these three have zero inbound
# links. Past versions remain in git history; only future churn is ignored.
obsidian_vault/Cross_Market_Arb.md
obsidian_vault/Cross_Market_Titans.md
obsidian_vault/Risk_Sentinel.md

# Autoresearch campaign worktree (a git worktree of quant_trading_lab on
# branch autoresearch/*; its own repo, not content of DEV).
qtl_autoresearch/

# Holdout verification worktree (git worktree of quant_trading_lab on
# branch holdout/*; its own repo, not content of DEV).
qtl_holdout/
qtl_c4_holdout/
qtl_*_holdout/
# DEFECT-ENG-001 fix worktree (git worktree of quant_trading_lab on bugfix/engine-slippage-signs)
qtl_slipfix/

# Credential modules -- never track secrets (AGENTS.md item 532)
*_key.py
*.key

# secrets: never track these (Section 93 s.7 - empty today, a hot-wallet key tomorrow)
dontshare.py
**/dontshare.py
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example
